WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.467
-Thank you so much.
Welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:04.534
-Thanks for having me back.
-Whenever.

00:00:04.534 --> 00:00:06.567
I got to say congratulations
to you.

00:00:06.567 --> 00:00:07.934
Since last I saw you,
you have a baby.

00:00:07.934 --> 00:00:09.300
-I know.
-A beautiful baby.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:11.133
Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:13.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:14.734
-Does he love it
when Mom sings to him?

00:00:14.734 --> 00:00:16.934
Do you sing lullabies?
-Oh.

00:00:16.934 --> 00:00:18.701
No.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.701 --> 00:00:21.067
No, he hates it.
-Baby doesn't like it at all?

00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:23.067
-No, he's my biggest critic.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:24.534
-He's like, "You gotta work on
that one."

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:27.467
-No, it's funny. My mom, she
can't carry a tune in a bucket.

00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:28.467
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:31.000
It's really bad,
and when she sings,

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.100
his eyes light up like she's
the stars and the moon.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.133
-He loves it.
[ Audience aws ]

00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:38.701
-But when I sing,
he's not a fan.

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:40.234
[ Laughter ]
-Is that, really?

00:00:40.234 --> 00:00:42.033
-Not a fan. I get the...

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:44.734
-Oh, no. Yeah, don't cry.

00:00:44.734 --> 00:00:46.334
Oh, no. I know that face.
-Yeah.

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:47.767
-Yeah, you're -- Oh.
-I'm like, "Alright. Okay."

00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:49.767
Most kids would be really happy.

00:00:49.767 --> 00:00:51.400
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.767
-Are you loving being on tour?

00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:54.467
This is the Love and Power Tour.

00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:57.067
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:57.067 --> 00:00:59.634
-I love the poster.
-Thank you.

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:01.133
Yeah, it's been really
incredible.

00:01:01.133 --> 00:01:04.167
It's been amazing.
I miss touring so much.

00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:05.934
And, you know, there was a
minute there where I didn't know

00:01:05.934 --> 00:01:08.000
if I was going to be able to do
it for a while.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.934
-Yeah.
-And being back on the road

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:13.868
and seeing people in the crowd
coming alive to the lyrics --

00:01:13.868 --> 00:01:15.767
-That's part of you.
-Yeah, it's incredible.

00:01:15.767 --> 00:01:17.267
-Your new single is "So Good,"
by the way.

00:01:17.267 --> 00:01:18.634
-Yeah.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:20.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:20.601 --> 00:01:21.767
-Thank you. Yeah.

00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:24.734
-"So Good."
-The name is really, really

00:01:24.734 --> 00:01:27.267
funny because when we're having
conversations about it,

00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:28.801
you know, I'll play it for
somebody and they'll be like,

00:01:28.801 --> 00:01:30.501
"Oh, it's so good."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:32.501
-You're like, "No, literally,
it's 'So Good.'"

00:01:32.501 --> 00:01:33.901
-That's exactly what it is.

00:01:33.901 --> 00:01:35.801
-Exactly, that's the name
of the song.

00:01:35.801 --> 00:01:37.834
But finally, the song is out.
-Yeah.

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:39.667
-Does it feel good that the song
is out?

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:41.601
-Yeah, it feels amazing.
I think as an artist,

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:44.100
you just want to be able
to release things. You know?

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:47.067
Like, music is such a cool
industry because you have

00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:50.467
the luxury to put stuff out
as soon as it comes to you,

00:01:50.467 --> 00:01:52.868
as soon as it's a thought
and a feeling

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:54.367
and it's current to the moment.

00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:57.067
So I was really, really keen to
just kind of get this out now

00:01:57.067 --> 00:01:58.934
while I was just feeling it.
-It's a beautiful love song.

00:01:58.934 --> 00:02:01.634
-Yeah, it is. I wrote it about
my partner love.

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:03.133
Yeah, I did.

00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:05.934
And he and I met in
a really cool way.

00:02:05.934 --> 00:02:07.300
-How?

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:10.367
-I met him in 2017

00:02:10.367 --> 00:02:13.067
and he was hired to write
a movie about me.

00:02:13.067 --> 00:02:15.634
-Ooh. Oh, that's right.
He's a director and a writer.

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:17.834
-Uh-huh. So he was hired to
write a movie about me,

00:02:17.834 --> 00:02:20.934
kind of like "8 Mile."
Less spaghetti.

00:02:20.934 --> 00:02:21.968
You know?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.968 --> 00:02:23.534
-Okay, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:23.534 --> 00:02:25.267
But I was going to wear
the cool hoodie, though.

00:02:25.267 --> 00:02:26.934
-Yeah, you have to.

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:28.801
-So he kind of followed me
around on tour.

00:02:28.801 --> 00:02:30.501
And he was interviewing me.

00:02:30.501 --> 00:02:33.133
And after a couple of years of
getting to know me,

00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:34.667
one day I kind of sat down
and I was like,

00:02:34.667 --> 00:02:36.033
"Hey, you know everything
about me.

00:02:36.033 --> 00:02:37.234
I don't know anything about you.

00:02:37.234 --> 00:02:39.567
I'm going to start interviewing
you back."

00:02:39.567 --> 00:02:42.300
And we found out that we had
so much in common.
-You fell in love.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:45.067
-After being friends for a long
time, we fell in love. Yeah.

00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:46.334
-That's the best way to do it.
-I know.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.133
-That's the best way to do it.
-I know.

00:02:48.133 --> 00:02:49.300
-Come on, congratulations.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:50.834
-Thank you.
-That's the best way to do it.

00:02:50.834 --> 00:02:52.767
To be friends, go like, "Hey, I
just want to hang out with you."

00:02:52.767 --> 00:02:54.834
-Yeah.
-What happened to the biopic?

00:02:54.834 --> 00:02:57.467
-Okay, well, there's a conflict
of interest now

00:02:57.467 --> 00:02:59.567
because he's a --
he's a main character.

00:02:59.567 --> 00:03:00.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.901 --> 00:03:03.100
But he got to direct
the music video instead,

00:03:03.100 --> 00:03:04.434
which was really cool.

00:03:04.434 --> 00:03:06.968
So it's kind of like a mini
taste of what could be.

00:03:06.968 --> 00:03:08.834
-I was thinking about
who could play you.

00:03:08.834 --> 00:03:10.234
-Oh, God.

00:03:10.234 --> 00:03:12.033
I know the answer.

00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:14.701
-Is it who I think it -- Ready?

00:03:14.701 --> 00:03:16.000
Here's who I think
should play you.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.267
Well, this is you.

00:03:17.267 --> 00:03:20.000
But this is you as
Millie Bobby Brown.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.734
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, I was going to say you.

00:03:22.734 --> 00:03:24.300
-Do you think I should play you?

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.801
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.801 --> 00:03:27.200
-What? No.
-No?

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:28.834
-Millie Bobby Brown
should play you. Yeah.

00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:30.267
-I mean, yeah, Millie
would be great.

00:03:30.267 --> 00:03:32.467
But I don't really think I'm
famous enough to cast Millie.

00:03:32.467 --> 00:03:33.534
You'll do it though, right?

00:03:33.534 --> 00:03:35.300
-Of course.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:39.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.868
-No, Millie would be so great.

00:03:41.868 --> 00:03:44.834
Millie -- I mean, it's kind of
uncanny how much we look alike.

00:03:44.834 --> 00:03:47.701
It's like, "Oh, no. We actually
just look like sisters."

00:03:47.701 --> 00:03:49.167
-Yeah, you really do.
-Yeah.

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:51.868
-I was just talking about you
because the great Adam Sandler

00:03:51.868 --> 00:03:53.467
was on our show last week.
-Aw!

00:03:53.467 --> 00:03:56.267
-And he loves you and he said
that -- he told me that you

00:03:56.267 --> 00:03:58.133
performed at his daughter's
bat mitzvah.

00:03:58.133 --> 00:04:00.067
-I did. I did. It was awesome.
[ Audience aws ]

00:04:00.067 --> 00:04:01.567
First of all, it was
the craziest bat mitzvah

00:04:01.567 --> 00:04:03.834
I've ever seen in my life.
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:03.834 --> 00:04:06.067
-As you would expect
from Adam Sandler.

00:04:06.067 --> 00:04:09.901
It was like -- I mean, it was
like Coachella.

00:04:09.901 --> 00:04:10.701
-Really?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:12.334
-I couldn't believe it.

00:04:12.334 --> 00:04:15.234
And also, I was like,
"Wow, you guys booked me?"

00:04:15.234 --> 00:04:18.467
I was really honored.
But his daughters are great.

00:04:18.467 --> 00:04:20.234
And he's so amazing.
-Oh, so cute.

00:04:20.234 --> 00:04:22.868
-It was a really cool
full-circle moment too because

00:04:22.868 --> 00:04:25.734
when I was a kid, his movies
used to play in my house

00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:27.100
all the time, right?
-Yeah.

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:30.367
-And my dad is a huge golfer
and loved "Happy Gilmore."

00:04:30.367 --> 00:04:32.033
He used to watch it
all the time.

00:04:32.033 --> 00:04:36.000
And so my first sentence that
I ever spoke in my life

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.033
was "Go home, ball."

00:04:38.033 --> 00:04:39.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:39.567 --> 00:04:41.000
Yeah.
-Is that right?

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:43.100
-Yeah, so I would run around
like a baby.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:44.267
Like, crawling around on
the floor.

00:04:44.267 --> 00:04:45.968
-"Go to your home."
-"Go to your home, ball."

00:04:45.968 --> 00:04:47.300
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:48.634
-That's the best.
-Yeah.

00:04:48.634 --> 00:04:50.767
-That's your first sentence?
-Yeah.

00:04:50.767 --> 00:04:52.801
-I want to talk about
your new makeup line.

00:04:52.801 --> 00:04:55.434
-Oh, yeah, about-face.
It's, like, the best --

00:04:55.434 --> 00:04:57.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:57.501 --> 00:05:00.634
-This is something --
-The best idea I ever had.

00:05:00.634 --> 00:05:02.634
-Speaking of something
that you can't just do

00:05:02.634 --> 00:05:03.834
and have it come out
the same week,

00:05:03.834 --> 00:05:07.467
this takes years of work
and research and stuff.

00:05:07.467 --> 00:05:09.167
So much work goes into it.
-It is. Yeah.

00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:12.701
Also, like, I'm a little --
I don't know.

00:05:12.701 --> 00:05:13.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.601 --> 00:05:14.767
-Say it.

00:05:14.767 --> 00:05:16.667
-Neurotic.
-Yeah.

00:05:16.667 --> 00:05:17.968
Like, controlling?

00:05:17.968 --> 00:05:20.434
-Nnnn, in a good way.

00:05:20.434 --> 00:05:22.701
I want everything to be perfect
all of the time, you know?

00:05:22.701 --> 00:05:24.467
-Wow.
-So, I really spent a lot

00:05:24.467 --> 00:05:28.834
of time just, like, meticulously
working on the formulas.

00:05:28.834 --> 00:05:30.501
-Like, how nerdy do you get
when it comes to it?

00:05:30.501 --> 00:05:32.167
-Ooh, nerdy.
-Really?

00:05:32.167 --> 00:05:34.567
-Yeah. "This has too much
hyaluronic acid.

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:35.934
We need to reduce the amount

00:05:35.934 --> 00:05:37.634
because the formula's
too creamy." Yeah.

00:05:37.634 --> 00:05:39.434
-Are you wearing
a lab coat and goggles?

00:05:39.434 --> 00:05:40.868
-I literally am acting like

00:05:40.868 --> 00:05:44.868
I'm trying to, like, cure
a disease in my basement.

00:05:44.868 --> 00:05:48.200
-And you're making makeup just
to make everyone feel better?

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.434
-Yeah. It's tough, though,
because I'm a musician,

00:05:50.434 --> 00:05:52.067
so I'm on stage.

00:05:52.067 --> 00:05:56.234
So my products need to be
so long wear, so good,

00:05:56.234 --> 00:05:58.234
so high performance
because if I get on stage

00:05:58.234 --> 00:06:00.467
and my lipstick starts smearing
all over the place,

00:06:00.467 --> 00:06:02.133
people are like,
"I'm not buying that."

00:06:02.133 --> 00:06:03.400
-Exactly. Yeah, of course.
-You know?

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:04.567
-It's got to work.
-Yeah.

00:06:04.567 --> 00:06:06.667
-Congrats on about-face.
Congrats on the tour.

00:06:06.667 --> 00:06:08.567
-Thank you.
-Congrats on the new music.

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:10.167
And, of course,
congrats on baby.

00:06:10.167 --> 00:06:11.133
That's the greatest.
-Aw, thank you so much.

00:06:11.133 --> 00:06:12.334
-Halsey, everybody.

00:06:12.334 --> 00:06:13.601
[ Cheers and applause ]
We love you.

00:06:13.601 --> 00:06:16.100
Halsey and I are playing
"The Best Friends Challenge"

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:17.467
when we come back.
Stick around.

